        {
          "id": "gs-08-keep-going",
          "title": "Lesson 8: Where to go next",
          "durationMinutes": 6,
          "overview": "You have installed an app, used it, backed it up and restored it. That same pattern works for any RobOS app. Here is what to try next, what to do before using a till for real, and where to get help.",
          "body": "## The pattern you now know\n\nWhichever app you try next, the same steps apply:\n\n1. Install it from App Manager.\n2. Try it with sample or throwaway data.\n3. Find out where it saves its work, and whether Config Sync covers it.\n4. Prove you can get that work back, before you rely on it.\n\n## What to try next\n\n| If you are... | Try | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Running a shop, café or bar | [Point of Sale guides](https://rowbose.com/point-of-sale/) | Tabs, stock, refunds and a customer self-checkout |\n| Looking after a car, or a repair shop | Auto Center | Maintenance records, recalls and invoices |\n| Keeping a music collection | Audio Player | A local library, plus Google Cast speakers |\n| Managing passwords | Pass Manager | An encrypted password vault that stays on your machine |\n| Learning how a family's finances fit together | RobOS Household | A safe sandbox with invented data, not for real records |\n| Writing software | [Build apps](https://rowbose.com/build-apps/) | The plan, build and review loop from lesson 7 |\n\nBrowse everything in the [App Directory](https://rowbose.com/apps/), or use **Search apps** in App Manager. Its **Updates** view shows what has a new version, and **Apply updates** installs it.\n\n## Before you use Point of Sale for real\n\nBean There Coffee was practice. A real shop needs more care:\n\n- **Change every PIN.** Anyone who has read this course knows `1111`. Manage your team under **Team & API**.\n- **Set your own details** under **Settings**: business name, address, and your local currency.\n- **Set the correct tax rates** under **Menu & Catalog**, then **Taxes**. The 8.5% here is an invented sample. Check with an accountant.\n- **Replace the sample menu** with your own, and remove what you don't sell.\n- **Understand card payments.** Cash is built in. For cards, the app either records an approval code from a separate card terminal, or uses a test gateway that never charges anyone. It does not process real cards by itself.\n- **Back up with a passphrase,** and do a test restore, as in lesson 5.\n- **Run it alongside your old system for a while.** This is young software, and your shop's takings depend on it.\n\n## Getting help\n\n- **[Discord](https://discord.gg/6PjxzkHujE)** for questions.\n- **[GitHub issues](https://github.com/nddipiazza/robos/issues)** for bugs and requests. Say what you did, what you expected, and what happened instead.\n\n## More courses, and writing your own\n\nThe **RobOS eLearning** app, available in App Manager, runs courses like this one on your desktop. It saves your progress to `~/.config/robos/elearning/progress.json`. On this website, your progress stays in this browser.\n\n![The RobOS eLearning library, listing the available courses](/assets/elearning/library.jpg)\n\nCourses are stored as text in the knowledge graph, so they can be edited. In the app, **Edit course** opens the editor, the **⋯** menu on each lesson offers **Copy as Markdown** and **Export as HTML Zip**, and **Export website** turns a course into a web page you can host yourself. There's more on the [eLearning page](https://rowbose.com/elearning/).\n\nFinish the course and you can save a certificate as a PDF. On this website, that takes at least 80% of the labs and quizzes, including 80% of the quiz questions. In the app, it takes all of them. A certificate records that you finished this course, and it isn't a formal qualification.\n",
          "keyPoints": [
            "Install, try with sample data, find the data, prove you can restore it.",
            "Before real use: change the PINs, set real taxes and back up with a passphrase.",
            "Ask on Discord, and report bugs on GitHub with what you did and what happened."
          ],
          "labSteps": [
            "Try the app you picked in lesson 1.",
            "Tidy up, or keep going."
          ],
          "labDetails": [
            {
              "description": "Install the app you noted in lesson 1. Spend ten minutes with it, then answer this: where does it save its work?",
              "expected": "You have the app open, and you can find its folder under `~/.config/robos/`. If you can't find one, ask on Discord before trusting it with anything important."
            },
            {
              "description": "Keep Bean There Coffee to play with if you like. To remove it from this computer, first uninstall Point of Sale in App Manager, then delete the `~/.config/robos/point-of-sale` folder yourself, since uninstalling keeps it. Do the same for your practice vault and `~/pos-practice` if you made them. Check that you are deleting the right thing, because this can't be undone.",
              "expected": "Either you still have your practice shop, or opening a reinstalled Point of Sale shows the welcome screen again."
            }
          ],
          "quiz": [
            {
              "question": "You are about to use Point of Sale in your real shop. What must you change first?",
              "options": [
                "Every sample PIN, since 1111 is published in this course",
                "The app's colors, so that staff can recognize it",
                "Nothing, because the sample data clears itself",
                "The folder that the app saves its data file in"
              ],
              "answer": "Every sample PIN, since 1111 is published in this course",
              "explanation": "The sample PINs are public, so anyone could sign in as the owner. Tax rates and the menu also need to be yours."
            },
            {
              "question": "A customer wants to pay by card. What does Point of Sale do out of the box?",
              "options": [
                "It records an approval from a separate card terminal",
                "It charges the card directly over your internet line",
                "It stores the card number and charges it at closing",
                "It sends the customer a RobOS payment link to use"
              ],
              "answer": "It records an approval from a separate card terminal",
              "explanation": "The manual provider records the approval code from a standalone terminal. The app never sees or stores card numbers, and the other built-in provider is a test gateway."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "robos:modulesCount": 8,
