        {
          "id": "mod-05-clean-room-art-and-godot-engine",
          "title": "Module 5: Clean-Room Art (jrpg-generate-art) and the 4-Hero Godot 4.3 Engine (ff1-game)",
          "durationMinutes": 25,
          "overview": "Generating 50 clean-room NES-quantized assets with jrpg-generate-art, publishing the clean graph to ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public, and building the 4-hero Godot 4.3 project (GameState.gd, TitleScreen.gd, PartyCreate.gd, FF1MapScene.gd, and GameControlServer.gd on port 8090).",
          "lessonHtml": "<div class=\"lesson-section\"><h4 class=\"lesson-subtitle\">Generating 50 clean-room assets and publishing the clean graph</h4><p class=\"lesson-text\">With our 1,206-node Knowledge Graph complete, we run the <code>.agents/skills/jrpg-generate-art/SKILL.md</code> pipeline (<code>jrpg-parser.js plan</code>, <code>art</code>, and <code>publish</code>). Using <code>packages/robos-lib/ai-image.js</code> and <code>packages/robos-jrpg-parser/tools/nesify.py</code> (which quantizes generated images to the 54-color NES hardware palette and strips backgrounds), we generated <strong>50 clean-room assets</strong> in <code>~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes/assets/generated/</code>—including all 12 character class battle sprites, 5 battle backdrops, 28 area maps, 4 menu screens, and the world map.</p><p class=\"lesson-text\">Running <code>jrpg-parser.js publish --out ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes --to ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public</code> then writes a redistributable copy containing <strong>1,184 fact nodes and 50 clean-room images</strong>, with every source filename, SHA-256 reference hash, and verbatim walkthrough quote stripped out.</p></div>\n<div class=\"lesson-section\"><h4 class=\"lesson-subtitle\">Architecture of the 4-hero Godot 4.3 project (~/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game)</h4><p class=\"lesson-text\">Next, <code>~/Downloads/ff1/build_ff1_godot_game.py</code> generates the complete Godot 4.3 (<code>gl_compatibility</code>) project in <code>~/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game</code>:</p><ul style=\"margin:0 0 12px 20px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.7;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong><code>scripts/GameState.gd</code>:</strong> Autoload singleton holding the 4 Light Warriors (<code>ZEST</code> Fighter, <code>SAIL</code> Thief, <code>ROBO</code> White Mage, <code>MAGE</code> Black Mage) with exact NES Level 1 stats, <code>400 Gold</code>, per-hero weapon/armor/spell lists, <code>opened_chests</code>, and story flags (<code>party_created</code>, <code>talked_coneria_guard</code>, <code>bought_weapon_coneria</code>, <code>bought_armor_coneria</code>, <code>bought_white_magic_coneria</code>, <code>bought_black_magic_coneria</code>, <code>king_intro_done</code>, <code>garland_defeated</code>, <code>princess_rescued</code>, <code>bridge_built</code>).</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong><code>scripts/TitleScreen.gd</code> &amp; <code>scripts/PartyCreate.gd</code>:</strong> The classic blue-bordered prologue screen and the 4-slot party creation screen that transitions into <code>res://scenes/Coneria.tscn</code> at <code>Vector2i(16, 21)</code>.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong><code>scripts/FF1MapScene.gd</code>:</strong> Shared map, dialogue, 2-step Shop interior, treasure chest, and turn-based 4-hero vs monster combat controller across <code>Coneria</code>, <code>WorldMap</code>, <code>ConeriaCastle1F</code>, <code>ConeriaCastle2F</code>, and <code>TempleOfFiends</code>.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom:6px;\"><strong><code>scripts/GameControlServer.gd</code>:</strong> Non-blocking TCP HTTP/JSON bridge on <code>127.0.0.1:8090</code> exposing <code>GET /api/v1/state</code>, <code>POST /api/v1/input</code>, and <code>POST /api/v1/command</code> (including <code>export_save_state</code> and <code>import_save_state</code> for milestone checkpoints).</li></ul></div>",
          "labSteps": [
            "Publish the clean-room Knowledge Graph and verify zero source leaks",
            "Generate ~/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game and run godot4 --headless --import",
            "Boot the game headlessly and inspect the 4 Light Warriors over port 8090"
          ],
          "labDetails": [
            {
              "title": "Publish the clean-room Knowledge Graph and verify zero source leaks",
              "who": "Your AI agent runs a program",
              "description": "Run jrpg-parser.js publish to export ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public and verify that no StrategyWiki, VGMaps, or manual filenames remain in the public folder.",
              "agentPrompt": "Run node packages/robos-jrpg-parser/bin/jrpg-parser.js publish --out ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes --to ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public and verify with grep that no source filenames appear in the exported folder.",
              "explain": "The publish command copies only validated fact nodes and clean-room generated images into the target directory while stripping provenance filenames, hashes, and verbatim quotes.",
              "code": "node packages/robos-jrpg-parser/bin/jrpg-parser.js publish \\\n  --out ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes --to ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public\ngrep -rn \"StrategyWiki\\|VGMaps\\|CLV-P\" ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public/ | wc -l",
              "expected": "The parser writes 1,184 nodes and 50 clean-room generated images to ~/kgraphs/final-fantasy-nes-public, and grep returns 0 matches for any source filename.",
              "image": "/assets/elearning/jrpg-kgraph/part2/m5-s1-clean-room-art-sheet.png"
            },
            {
              "title": "Generate ~/Downloads/ff1/ff1-game and run godot4 --headless --import",
